1826	> Why `pruned.len() == pool.len()` is the "unchanged" test: `prune` either returns a strict subset (the predicate disproved at least one), or the original pool (no disproof, or prune-to-empty). Comparing lengths is sufficient because `prune` never reorders-without-removing — a same-length result is the original pool object. A single-element bare pool that the predicate "keeps" also returns unchanged here (len 1 == len 1 → `None`), so it correctly falls through to `owner_lookup_in_modules`, which mints the singleton Exact. This avoids double-handling the trivial singleton.
